1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,912
Welcome to Module Eight.

2
00:00:01,912 --> 00:00:05,125
Synthetic biologists like to ask a blunt question.

3
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:08,812
What is the smallest set of parts that still counts as alive?

4
00:00:08,812 --> 00:00:11,050
A minimal cell needs a boundary.

5
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:12,412
A way to sense.

6
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:13,687
A way to act.

7
00:00:13,687 --> 00:00:16,175
A metabolism that keeps cycling.

8
00:00:16,175 --> 00:00:18,062
And some way to persist.

9
00:00:18,062 --> 00:00:20,287
Today you build the minimal agent.

10
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:25,425
Yesterday you saw that every real coding agent is built from the same seven parts.

11
00:00:25,425 --> 00:00:31,387
Today you write the smallest thing that still has the essential ones, in about a hundred lines of Python.

12
00:00:31,387 --> 00:00:33,450
It is smaller than you might expect.

13
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:39,450
One research agent, used as a baseline in serious studies, is roughly a hundred lines.

14
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:45,325
A loop, one prompt, one tool, a growing list of messages, and two limits.

15
00:00:45,325 --> 00:00:46,362
That is it.

16
00:00:46,362 --> 00:00:49,375
The secret is that tools are just text.

17
00:00:49,375 --> 00:00:52,525
The model reads a short description of each tool.

18
00:00:52,525 --> 00:00:59,125
When it wants one, it writes a small piece of structured text that says, use this tool, with these settings.

19
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:05,000
Your code reads that, runs the real function, and pastes the result back into the conversation.

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,987
Then the model reads everything again, including the new result, and decides what to do next.

21
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:14,012
One writer took minimalism to an extreme.

22
00:01:14,012 --> 00:01:21,487
His experiment, called Ouro, gives a model one instruction and one tool, the ability to run code inside its own editor.

23
00:01:21,487 --> 00:01:25,462
The model's first job is to rewrite itself into a proper loop.

24
00:01:25,462 --> 00:01:26,837
And it does.

25
00:01:26,837 --> 00:01:30,500
Then it keeps going, building new features onto itself.

26
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:35,550
It is a lovely demonstration of how little a capable model needs to grow a whole system.

27
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,225
But read his warning.

28
00:01:37,225 --> 00:01:38,887
There are no guardrails.

29
00:01:38,887 --> 00:01:42,675
Nothing stops it from breaking itself, or anything else.

30
00:01:42,675 --> 00:01:45,950
He says to run it only inside a sealed container.

31
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:49,050
And that is where today's metaphor fails.

32
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:51,312
A minimal cell limits itself.

33
00:01:51,312 --> 00:01:57,100
It can only use what reaches its membrane, and if something goes wrong, it dies quietly.

34
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,950
A minimal agent has no such limits.

35
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:07,312
Give it a command line and it can delete a folder, leak a password, or send an email, and it will not stop to reflect.

36
00:02:07,312 --> 00:02:09,150
It just calls the next tool.

37
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:11,987
In biology, the boundary comes first.

38
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:14,550
In agents, people tend to add it last.

39
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:15,962
You will add it first.

40
00:02:15,962 --> 00:02:21,137
So in today's lab, your agent gets only tools that read, never write.

41
00:02:21,137 --> 00:02:25,237
Each tool refuses any path outside the one folder you allow.

42
00:02:25,237 --> 00:02:28,087
There is a hard limit of eight turns.

43
00:02:28,087 --> 00:02:32,612
And every turn is written to a small log file, so you can see exactly what it did.

44
00:02:32,612 --> 00:02:39,237
For the model itself, you will use your coding agent's headless mode, so you do not need any new paid service.

45
00:02:39,237 --> 00:02:45,012
Then you will grow it a third tool, and test the boundary by asking it to read something it should never see.

46
00:02:45,012 --> 00:02:49,325
If the boundary holds, you have a minimal organism that is safe to keep.

47
00:02:49,325 --> 00:02:51,962
Open your terminal, and let's build one.

